== Current sequence

The current ordering is W0--W10 in `docs/process/backlog-graph.typ`. W1 (IR contract)
and W2 (general handlers) are the next language roots; W3 unifies F\#/Elixir
package calls under `logic`; W4 is self-hosting and self-typing; W5 hardens hot
swap; W6/W7 are host surfaces; W8 is the verification bridge; W9 is
security/Nu/performance; W10/W0 are product and release gates. The graph, not
this paragraph, is the authority.

== Read budget

Read `docs/now.typ` first. Then read the active W item, the specification section,
the feature document, and the decision-index row for the active decision. Use
`doc_get_section` for one decision or archive section. Do not read
`docs/process/decision-records.typ` or `docs/archive/roadmap-archive.typ` end to end; they are
evidence, not a briefing.
